"Dijkstra benchmark (dict as priority queue, design note
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-12-dict-design.md §7 and §10 item 3).
Shortest path across a synthetic 141 by 141 grid from [0, 0] to
[140, 140], moving to the four neighbours, paying the weight of each cell
entered: ((7x + 13y + xy) mod 9) + 1. The queue is a dict keyed by
`[distance, [x, y]]` (unique, so no sequence number is needed), taken in
order with `dict.pop-min`; best distances are a dict keyed by `[x, y]`.
Stale queue entries are skipped when popped.

Expected distance computed independently (Python, heapq): 1085."

` "the side of the grid"
n: 141

` "a distance longer than any path"
far: 1000000000

` "the target cell"
goal: [n - 1, n - 1]

` "the weight of the cell `[x, y]`"
weight([x, y]): (7 * x + 13 * y + x * y) % 9 + 1

` "true if the cell `[x, y]` is on the grid"
inside?([x, y]): x >= 0 ∧ x < n ∧ y >= 0 ∧ y < n

` "the cells next to `[x, y]` on the grid"
neighbours([x, y]): [[x + 1, y], [x - 1, y], [x, y + 1], [x, y - 1]] filter(inside?)

` "the cost of entering cell `c` from a cell at distance `d`"
via(d, c): d + weight(c)

` "true if entering cell `c` at distance `d` beats its best distance so far in `dist`"
better?(d, dist, c): via(d, c) < (dist dict.get-or(c, far))

` "queue cell `c`, entered from a cell at distance `d`"
push(d, queue, c): queue dict.assoc([via(d, c), c], null)

` "record the distance of cell `c`, entered from a cell at distance `d`"
record(d, dist, c): dist dict.assoc(c, via(d, c))

` "take the nearest queued cell and continue the search from it"
search(queue, dist): queue dict.pop-min visit(dist)

` "visit cell `c` at distance `d`, with `rest` still queued: a stale entry (`c` already reached by a shorter path) relaxes nothing"
visit(dist, [[d, c], v, rest]): {
  fresh: d <= (dist dict.get-or(c, far))
  improved: fresh then(c neighbours filter(better?(d, dist)), [])
}.((c = goal) then(d, search(improved foldl(push(d), rest), improved foldl(record(d), dist))))

` :suppress
start-queue: dict.of[[[0, [0, 0]], null]]

` :suppress
start-dist: dict.of[[[0, 0], 0]]

` { target: :bench-dict-dijkstra
    verify: ["default-expectation"] }
bench-dict-dijkstra: {
  distance: search(start-queue, start-dist)
  RESULT: (distance = 1085) then(:PASS, :FAIL)
}
